 "notes": "Hidden-photon (dark photon) dark matter search with a fixed-frequency superconducting lumped-element resonator (DM Radio test device). Headline result is the 90% C.L. exclusion on kinetic mixing angle epsilon vs hidden photon mass, Fig. 3a. Curve traced by pixel analysis of the embedded raster image of panel a (axes calibrated from tick marks: x = 2.031/2.035/2.039 neV, y = 1..5 in units of 1e-9). V-shaped curve minimum epsilon ~ 1.5e-9 at 2.035 neV, consistent with the text statement 'excluding kinetic mixing angles of epsilon >~ 1.5e-9 in a band around 2.035 neV'. Mass converted neV->eV (x1e-9); coupling reported as chi (=epsilon), not chi^2. Normalized to local DM density rho_DM = 0.45 GeV/cm^3 (paper's assumption, not rescaled). Limit assumes hidden-photon effective current along the shield longitudinal axis; field disalignment would weaken it.",
